302:{"timestamp":"2026-07-22T05:27:05.107Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0ed6f27ae2a1b06c016a6054671674819097a31dd919cb3fc5","status":"completed","call_id":"call_k8kKYUimWX6UBDrGxMKN4kro","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /work/PROOF.md\\n+VALIDATED\\n+\\n+## What is proven\\n+\\n+Under the supplied `MPY` reference semantics, the translated `valid_date`\\n+function is partially correct for every value represented by `str(IntSeq)`.\\n+It returns `true` exactly when the input consists of ten code points in the\\n+form `mm-dd-yyyy`, all eight non-separator positions are ASCII decimal digits,\\n+the month is 1 through 12, the day is at least 1, and the day does not exceed\\n+29 for February, 30 for April/June/September/November, or 31 otherwise.\\n+\\n+The claims also constrain the operational state: the module definition is\\n+loaded from an initially empty module scope; the call restores environment 0,\\n+scope allocator 1, empty heap, heap allocator 0, empty stack, `noRet`,\\n+`NoExc`, and exit code 0. The loaded `valid_date` module binding remains.\\n+\\n+This is a reachability/partial-correctness result. It is not a separate\\n+termination theorem or a proof of the supplied reference semantics against all\\n+of CPython.\\n+\\n+## Formal claim\\n+\\n+`spec.k` divides the complete `IntSeq` input algebra into two cases:\\n+\\n+1. `SPEC.invalid-length` universally quantifies `CS:IntSeq` under\\n+   `isLen(CS) =/=Int 10` and proves the result is `false`.\\n+2. `SPEC.length-ten` explicitly matches ten arbitrary symbolic code points\\n+   `C0` through `C9` and proves the result is\\n+   `validDate10(C0, ..., C9)`.\\n+\\n+Every finite `IntSeq` either has the displayed ten-constructor shape or has a\\n+length different from ten, so the two claims cover every formal string input.\\n+`validDate10` is an executable mathematical spelling of the prompt's format\\n+and month/day bounds. No loop or recursive source construct is present, so no\\n+loop circularity or invariant claim is required.\\n+\\n+## Proof-extension inventory\\n+\\n+All extensions are in `verification.k`. None is an operational bridge, a\\n+trusted primitive, a simplification lemma, or an opaque function.\\n+\\n+| Extension | Class | Semantic role and domain | State footprint | Justification and dependents | Validation |\\n+|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n+| `validDateProgram` equation | Definitional summary | Names the exact `Module(FuncDef(...))`; singleton/nullary domain; does not replace execution | None | The fixed `#loadAll` and `FuncDef` rules still execute; both target claims depend on it | LLVM execution of this alias and `solution.mpy` produced byte-for-byte equal final configurations |\\n+| `validDateBody` equation | Definitional summary | Names the exact translated statement sequence; singleton/nullary domain | None | Its value is installed in the closure and every statement executes under `MPY`; both target claims depend on it | Exact program-identity check passed; an always-false body mutation made its expected true result fail |\\n+| `validDateClosure` equation | Definitional summary | Names `closureVal((\\\"date\\\", .ParamNames), validDateBody, 0)`; singleton/nullary domain | None | Pins parameter, body, and defining environment; both claims depend on it | Final scopes from translated program and alias were identical |\\n+| `dateDigit(C)` | Definitional summary | All `C:Int`; one unconditional equation `C -Int 48` | None | Decimal code conversion in the postcondition; `dateTwoDigits`, `badDateDigit`, and `validDate10` depend on it | One equation gives total coverage, no overlap, and immediate termination |\\n+| `dateTwoDigits(A,B)` | Definitional summary | All integer pairs; one unconditional decimal equation | None | Names the two-digit month/day value; `validDate10` depends on it | Total, non-overlapping, and reduces to integer arithmetic |\\n+| `badDateDigit(C)` | Definitional summary | All `C:Int`; true exactly outside decoded 0 through 9 | None | Names the source digit guard; `validDate10` depends on it | Total, non-overlapping, and reduces to integer comparisons |\\n+| `validDate10(C0,...,C9)` | Definitional summary | All ten-integer tuples; one unconditional nested conditional | None | States separator, digit, month, and day requirements; `SPEC.length-ten` depends on it | Total and non-overlapping; finite independent oracle test reported zero mismatches |\\n+\\n+The equations are acyclic: program aliases terminate immediately;\\n+`validDate10` calls only `badDateDigit` and `dateTwoDigits`, which descend to\\n+`dateDigit`, which is arithmetic. Every `[total]` declaration has one\\n+unconditional equation, so coverage is complete and there are no pairwise\\n+guard overlaps.\\n+\\n+## Exact commands and actual outputs\\n+\\n+The complete reproducible command sequence is `./prove.sh`. Its final run\\n+exited 0. The central commands and observed results were:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+python3 py2mpy.py solution.py > solution.mpy\\n+# Exit: 0\\n+\\n+kompile reference-semantics/semantics.k \\\\\\n+  --backend llvm \\\\\\n+  --main-module MPY-KRUN \\\\\\n+  --syntax-module MPY-SYNTAX \\\\\\n+  --output-definition runtime-kompiled\\n+# Exit: 0; compiler emitted existing non-exhaustiveness/unused-variable warnings\\n+\\n+python3 py2mpy.py concrete_tests.py > concrete_tests.mpy\\n+krun concrete_tests.mpy --definition runtime-kompiled\\n+# Exit: 0\\n+# Final: <k> .K </k>, <exc> NoExc </exc>, <exit-code> 0 </exit-code>\\n+\\n+python3 differential_test.py\\n+# Output: cases=30923 mismatches=0\\n+# Exit: 0\\n+\\n+kompile --backend haskell verification.k \\\\\\n+  --main-module VERIFICATION \\\\\\n+  --syntax-module MPY-SYNTAX \\\\\\n+  --output-definition verification-kompiled\\n+# Exit: 0; only supplied-semantics unused-variable warnings\\n+\\n+kprove spec.k \\\\\\n+  --definition verification-kompiled \\\\\\n+  --spec-module SPEC\\n+# Output: #Top\\n+# Exit: 0\\n+```\\n+\\n+The program-identity check used the following builds/runs and printed the\\n+shown output:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+kompile --backend llvm verification.k \\\\\\n+  --main-module VERIFICATION \\\\\\n+  --syntax-module VERIFICATION \\\\\\n+  --output-definition verification-llvm-kompiled\\n+python3 - <<'PY'\\n+import subprocess\\n+\\n+def run(command):\\n+    return subprocess.run(\\n+        command, check=True, text=True, stdout=subprocess.PIPE\\n+    ).stdout\\n+\\n+translated = run([\\\"krun\\\", \\\"solution.mpy\\\", \\\"--definition\\\", \\\"runtime-kompiled\\\"])\\n+proof_alias = run(\\n+    [\\\"krun\\\", \\\"program_alias.mpy\\\", \\\"--definition\\\", \\\"verification-llvm-kompiled\\\"]\\n+)\\n+assert translated == proof_alias\\n+print(\\\"program identity: exact final configurations match\\\")\\n+PY\\n+# Output: program identity: exact final configurations match\\n+# Exit: 0\\n+```\\n+\\n+The two deliberate negative probes were:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+kprove spec-vacuity.k \\\\\\n+  --definition verification-kompiled \\\\\\n+  --spec-module SPEC-VACUITY\\n+# Exit: 1 (expected)\\n+# WarnStuckClaimState residual: <k> true ~> .K </k>, versus required false\\n+\\n+kprove spec-body-mutation.k \\\\\\n+  --definition verification-kompiled \\\\\\n+  --spec-module SPEC-BODY-MUTATION\\n+# Exit: 1 (expected)\\n+# WarnStuckClaimState residual: <k> false ~> .K </k>, versus required true\\n+```\\n+\\n+## Gate results\\n+\\n+### Gate A — PASS\\n+\\n+- A1: The claims load `validDateProgram`, resolve `valid_date` through the\\n+  module scope, evaluate the real argument, enter the exact closure, and\\n+  execute `validDateBody`. The translated module and proof alias produced\\n+  exact matching final configurations. Replacing the body with `return False`\\n+  invalidated the expected true result with exit 1.\\n+- A2: There are no operational bridges. All active state cells are present in\\n+  the claims and are restored or updated exactly as described above.\\n+- A3: Lookup, left-to-right call/argument evaluation, built-in resolution,\\n+  returns, frame push/pop, and exception state are handled only by fixed\\n+  semantics rules.\\n+- A4: Every proof-local equation is unconditional, total on its declared\\n+  domain, non-overlapping, acyclic, and terminating. No false off-path rule,\\n+  simplification axiom, priority rewrite, or opacity is present.\\n+- A5: `03-11-2000` is a realizable witness. The false-result mutation reached\\n+  `true`, stuck against `false`, and exited 1. The positive result and all\\n+  operational cells are constrained by the claims.\\n+\\n+### Gate B — PASS\\n+\\n+- B1: The source contract accepts a date string. The formal domain is every\\n+  `str(IntSeq)` and excludes non-string Python objects. The two claims are\\n+  exhaustive over that domain; there is no hidden length or character\\n+  precondition.\\n+- B2: The operations material to this program—code-point string length,\\n+  indexing, ASCII `'-'`, `ord`, integer arithmetic/comparison, Boolean\\n+  short-circuiting, calls, and returns—are explicitly modeled. The\\n+  implementation deliberately interprets `mm-dd-yyyy` digits as ASCII `0` to\\n+  `9`; other code points remain in-domain and are rejected.\\n+- B3: `validDate10` separately checks separators, all eight digits, month\\n+  bounds, the lower day bound, and the prompt's 29/30/31 upper bounds. The\\n+  source body's branch structure and this mathematical result definition agree\\n+  in the universal symbolic proof. The independent oracle provides additional\\n+  finite evidence, not the universal argument.\\n+- B4: Prompt examples and all stated rules match the implementation. February\\n+  29 is allowed for every four-digit year, exactly as the prompt says; no\\n+  unstated leap-year rule was added.\\n+\\n+### Gate C — PASS\\n+\\n+All trust assumptions and empirical checks are named below, and every cited\\n+artifact and exact command exists in the current directory. Formal proof,\\n+conditional trust, and finite evidence are kept separate.\\n+\\n+## Trust boundary\\n+\\n+| Unproved component | Why outside theorem / effect | Dependents | Evidence |\\n+|---|---|---|---|\\n+| Supplied `reference-semantics/semantics.k` and imported modules | Fixed foundation requested by the task; affects value, binding, control, state, exceptions, and termination model | Both target claims and all K executions | Concrete LLVM suite; symbolic body-sensitive proof; source files remained unmodified |\\n+| `py2mpy.py` and CPython AST parsing | Translation correctness from Python source to `.mpy` is outside the K reachability theorem; affects the whole program term | `solution.mpy`, concrete suite, program-identity link | Required translator command succeeded; concrete-test function AST exactly equals `solution.py`; translated program and proof alias load to identical configurations |\\n+| K v7.1.293 compiler, LLVM backend, Haskell backend, and prover | Trusted implementation of parsing, execution, simplification, SMT interaction, and proof search | All machine results | Independent LLVM/Haskell builds, positive `#Top`, and two discriminating non-zero probes |\\n+| Plain-language interpretation of `mm-dd-yyyy` as ASCII digits | Human-intent bridge, not a theorem about all possible date conventions | Gate B conclusion | Prompt notation/examples, explicit audited predicate, and independent regex/days-table oracle |\\n+\\n+There are no unproved proof-local operational primitives or lemmas.\\n+\\n+## Empirically supported facts\\n+\\n+- `concrete_tests.py` contains the identical `valid_date` AST plus 20 K\\n+  assertions covering all prompt examples, empty/wrong-format strings,\\n+  digit failures, zero bounds, February 29/30, 30-day month boundaries, and\\n+  31-day month boundaries. `krun` ended in `.K`, `NoExc`, exit code 0.\\n+- `differential_test.py` uses an independent ASCII regex and a month-to-days\\n+  table. Its 30,923 distinct inputs comprise all 100 month and 100 day fields\\n+  for years `0000`, `2000`, and `9999`; the prompt examples; every printable\\n+  ASCII single-position mutation of `03-11-2000`; and lengths 0 through 15.\\n+  Actual output was `cases=30923 mismatches=0`.\\n+- `spec-vacuity.k` and `spec-body-mutation.k` are negative proof artifacts;\\n+  both produced an explicit opposing Boolean residual and exited 1 as expected.\\n+\\n+Finite testing supports the source/semantics and intent bridges only. It is not\\n+reported as a universal proof.\\n+\\n+## Excluded behavior\\n+\\n+- Non-string arguments are outside the source and formal input domain; their\\n+  Python/K exception behavior is not claimed.\\n+- The theorem is relative to the supplied subset semantics. It does not claim\\n+  full semantic equivalence between that model and CPython.\\n+- Calendar rules absent from the prompt—leap-year validation, historical\\n+  calendars, time zones, or restrictions on the numeric year—are not claimed.\\n+- The proof is partial correctness and does not independently establish\\n+  termination, even though this implementation contains no loop or recursion.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019f883b-c88d-7250-bd0b-e723dc2eeef8"}}}
