RIFICATION \\\n  --syntax-module VERIFICATION \\\n  --output-definition verification-llvm-kompiled\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport subprocess\n\ndef run(command):\n    return subprocess.run(\n        command, check=True, text=True, stdout=subprocess.PIPE\n    ).stdout\n\ntranslated = run([\"krun\", \"solution.mpy\", \"--definition\", \"runtime-kompiled\"])\nproof_alias = run(\n    [\"krun\", \"program_alias.mpy\", \"--definition\", \"verification-llvm-kompiled\"]\n)\nassert translated == proof_alias\nprint(\"program identity: exact final configurations match\")\nPY\n# Output: program identity: exact final configurations match\n# Exit: 0\n```\n\nThe two deliberate negative probes were:\n\n```bash\nkprove spec-vacuity.k \\\n  --definition verification-kompiled \\\n  --spec-module SPEC-VACUITY\n# Exit: 1 (expected)\n# WarnStuckClaimState residual: <k> true ~> .K </k>, versus required false\n\nkprove spec-body-mutation.k \\\n  --definition verification-kompiled \\\n  --spec-module SPEC-BODY-MUTATION\n# Exit: 1 (expected)\n# WarnStuckClaimState residual: <k> false ~> .K </k>, versus required true\n```\n\n## Gate results\n\n### Gate A — PASS\n\n- A1: The claims load `validDateProgram`, resolve `valid_date` through the\n  module scope, evaluate the real argument, enter the exact closure, and\n  execute `validDateBody`. The translated module and proof alias produced\n  exact matching final configurations. Replacing the body with `return False`\n  invalidated the expected true result with exit 1.\n- A2: There are no operational bridges. All active state cells are present in\n  the claims and are restored or updated exactly as described above.\n- A3: Lookup, left-to-right call/argument evaluation, built-in resolution,\n  returns, frame push/pop, and exception state are handled only by fixed\n  semantics rules.\n- A4: Every proof-local equation is unconditional, total on its declared\n  domain, non-overlapping, acyclic, and terminating. No false off-path rule,\n  simplification axiom, priority rewrite, or opacity is present.\n- A5: `03-11-2000` is a realizable witness. The false-result mutation reached\n  `true`, stuck against `false`, and exited 1. The positive result and all\n  operational cells are constrained by the claims.\n\n### Gate B — PASS\n\n- B1: The source contract accepts a date string. The formal domain is every\n  `str(IntSeq)` and excludes non-string Python objects. The two claims are\n  exhaustive over that domain; there is no hidden length or character\n  precondition.\n- B2: The operations material to this program—code-point string length,\n  indexing, ASCII `'-'`, `ord`, integer arithmetic/comparison, Boolean\n  short-circuiting, calls, and returns—are explicitly modeled. The\n  implementation deliberately interprets `mm-dd-yyyy` digits as ASCII `0` to\n  `9`; other code points remain in-domain and are rejected.\n- B3: `validDate10` separately checks separators, all eight digits, month\n  bounds, the lower day bound, and the prompt's 29/30/31 upper bounds. The\n  source body's branch structure and this mathematical result definition agree\n  in the universal symbolic proof. The independent oracle provides additional\n  finite evidence, not the universal argument.\n- B4: Prompt examples and all stated rules match the implementation. February\n  29 is allowed for every four-digit year, exactly as the prompt says; no\n  unstated leap-year rule was added.\n\n### Gate C — PASS\n\nAll trust assumptions and empirical checks are named below, and every cited\nartifact and exact command exists in the current directory. Formal proof,\nconditional trust, and finite evidence are kept separate.\n\n## Trust boundary\n\n| Unproved component | Why outside theorem / effect | Dependents | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Supplied `reference-semantics/semantics.k` and imported modules | Fixed foundation requested by the task; affects value, binding, control, state, exceptions, and termination model | Both target claims and all K executions | Concrete LLVM suite; symbolic body-sensitive proof; source files remained unmodified |\n| `py2mpy.py` and CPython AST parsing | Translation correctness from Python source to `.mpy` is outside the K reachability theorem; affects the whole program term | `solution.mpy`, concrete suite, program-identity link | Required translator command succeeded; concrete-test function AST exactly equals `solution.py`; translated program and proof alias load to identical configurations |\n| K v7.1.293 compiler, LLVM backend, Haskell backend, and prover | Trusted implementation of parsing, execution, simplification, SMT interaction, and proof search | All machine results | Independent LLVM/Haskell builds, positive `#Top`, and two discriminating non-zero probes |\n| Plain-language interpretation of `mm-dd-yyyy` as ASCII digits | Human-intent bridge, not a theorem about all possible date conventions | Gate B conclusion | Prompt notation/examples, explicit audited predicate, and independent regex/days-table oracle |\n\nThere are no unproved proof-local operational primitives or lemmas.\n\n## Empirically supported facts\n\n- `concrete_tests.py` contains the identical `valid_date` AST plus 20 K\n  assertions covering all prompt examples, empty/wrong-format strings,\n  digit failures, zero bounds, February 29/30, 30-day month boundaries, and\n  31-day month boundaries. `krun` ended in `.K`, `NoExc`, exit code 0.\n- `differential_test.py` uses an independent ASCII regex and a month-to-days\n  table. Its 30,923 distinct inputs comprise all 100 month and 100 day fields\n  for years `0000`, `2000`, and `9999`; the prompt examples; every printable\n  ASCII single-position mutation of `03-11-2000`; and lengths 0 through 15.\n  Actual output was `cases=30923 mismatches=0`.\n- `spec-vacuity.k` and `spec-body-mutation.k` are negative proof artifacts;\n  both produced an explicit opposing Boolean residual and exited 1 as expected.\n\nFinite testing supports the source/semantics and intent bridges only